# V1 resources, actions, and sessions

<!-- Generated by scripts/generate-v1-guides.ts from executed canonical source. Do not edit this output by hand. -->

This guide shows the server-owned data and mutation model used by the
[canonical packed application](../../examples/v1-app/README.md). The files
below are executed directly by resource, action, packed-build, and three-browser
JavaScript-disabled tests.

## Request-owned resources

Declare a resource with `defineResource`, then read it through the page's
`context.read`. Equivalent structural inputs share one pending or settled value
inside one request. Results, failures, dependencies, and flow evidence are
released with that request; V1 has no cross-request result cache.

Expected application failures use `resourceError`. They reach the nearest
route error page with a stable code and status instead of becoming an internal
incident.

