## Typed native actions

`defineAction` owns bounded field decoding, mandatory authorization, session
mutation, redirects, and complete current-page revalidation. Only the action
callback receives a mutable session; pages and authorization receive the
read-only view. Rotating the session after a privilege change prevents the old
identity from continuing.

The example implements sign-in plus create, update, and delete operations.
Validation uses `actionError`, file input is bounded, and successful mutations
redirect only through the accepted same-origin outcome.

<!-- fadeno:include {"path":"examples/v1-app/src/projects.ts","language":"ts"} -->

## Render forms with generated identities

The action declaration is the form action and its field tokens are form-control
names. The framework generates the action proof and verifies it before running
application behavior. The page does not construct or parse those identities.

<!-- fadeno:include {"path":"examples/v1-app/src/routes/projects/page.tsx","language":"tsx"} -->

## Verify the workflow

Run `pnpm check:v1-running-example`. The packed HTTPS application signs in,
rotates its protected session, refuses invalid input, uploads a bounded text
file, creates/reads/updates/deletes a project, refuses replay, and proves stale
validation and stale project output disappear. Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit
run the essential flow with JavaScript disabled.

See [diagnostics and recovery](diagnostics-recovery.md) for normalized failure,
correction, flow, and recovery evidence.
